-- title:
--   Φ[p^N] as a Hopf algebra with mathcal O_D-coaction
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be prime, $B$ a commutative ring and $\Phi$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$: a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $B$ together with series endomorphisms $\Phi.\mathrm{act}\,a$ for $a$ in $\mathbb Z_{p^2} = W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$ and $\Phi.\mathrm{varpi}$, all law endomorphisms of $F$, with $\mathrm{act}\,1$ the identity, $\mathrm{act}(ab)$ the composite, $\mathrm{act}(a+b)$ the sum via $F$, $\mathrm{varpi}\circ\mathrm{varpi} = \mathrm{act}\,p$ and $\mathrm{varpi}\circ\mathrm{act}\,a = \mathrm{act}(\varphi a)\circ\mathrm{varpi}$. Fix $N$, write $\phi = \Phi.\mathrm{act}((p)^N)$ and let $I$ be the ideal of $B[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ generated by the two components of $\phi$; assume the quotient `KerAlgebra` $B[\![X]\!]/I$ is finite and free over $B$ and that each $X_i$ is nilpotent in it. Then there exist a commutative ring $L$ with a cocommutative Hopf $B$-algebra structure, free and finite as a $B$-module, and a surjective $B$-algebra map $\pi : B[\![X_0,X_1]\!]\to L$ with $\ker\pi = I$, with $\operatorname{finrank}_B L = \operatorname{finrank}_B(B[\![X]\!]/I)$, with each $\pi(X_i)$ nilpotent, with $\pi G$ the adic evaluation of $G$ at $(\pi(X_i))$ for the zero ideal of $L$, with $\Delta(\pi(X_i))$ the adic evaluation of $F_i$ at $(\pi(X_j)\otimes 1,\,1\otimes\pi(X_j))$ for the zero ideal of $L\otimes_B L$, with $\varepsilon(\pi(X_i)) = 0$ and $\varepsilon(\pi G)$ the constant coefficient of $G$, and such that for every $a \in \mathbb Z_{p^2}$ there is a bialgebra endomorphism $\rho$ of $L$ with $\rho(\pi G) = \pi(G\circ\mathrm{act}\,a)$ for all $G$, and likewise a bialgebra endomorphism $\varpi$ of $L$ with $\varpi(\pi G) = \pi(G\circ\Phi.\mathrm{varpi})$.
--
--   This exhibits the $p^N$-torsion $\Phi[p^N]$ of a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module as a finite free commutative cocommutative Hopf algebra over $B$, together with the coaction of $\mathcal O_D = \mathbb Z_{p^2}[\Pi]$ by bialgebra endomorphisms. It is the algebraic input to the construction of the finite flat group scheme $\Phi[p^N]$ and its projective embedding in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_scheme_represents_subgroup_ideal_and_isClosedImmersion_toProjSpace`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_scheme_represents_subgroup_ideal_and_isClosedImmersion_toProjSpace); the first eight clauses specialise the corresponding statement for a commutative formal group law, the remaining two adding functoriality in $\mathcal O_D$.
